Native Ubuntu 26.10 preview
==========================

This packaging targets Ubuntu 26.10 (stonking), initially amd64. It uses the
distribution's development/runtime libraries, not binaries copied from Flatpak.
Other Ubuntu/Debian versions have not been accepted. TNEF is explicitly enabled;
the elected application copy remains GPL-3.0-only with separate component terms.

Build from a clean source snapshot containing debian/ and all intended patches:

    sudo apt-get build-dep .
    DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS=parallel=6 dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc

The .deb, optional debug-symbol .ddeb, .buildinfo and .changes are written to the
parent directory. No source/binary publication or APT repository is configured.
Maintainer: Markus Kainer (D3rPaPaH0d3n), projekt@kainer.co.at.

The build runs the existing engine, focused helper and notification-flag tests,
plus desktop/AppStream validation. debian/run-tests.py isolates HOME/XDG,
network, process namespace and buses with Bubblewrap and a private D-Bus session.
A second isolated command exercises the real GTK contact-picture widgets with
synthetic local HTTPS/proxy fixtures, consent and malformed-response cases.
General WebKit/provider and personal-mail workflows require separate desktop
acceptance. No real mail, contacts, accounts or keyring is used.

The Ubuntu -Bsymbolic-functions linker option is removed in debian/rules:
the inherited static engine is linked into both executables and the private
client library, so local function binding duplicates GType registration.
Normal symbol interposition avoids that error. Other hardening remains enabled.

After inspecting the candidate and agreeing how existing accounts are handled,
installation uses the ordinary local-package command:

    sudo apt install ./griabuntu-mail_<version>_amd64.deb

The package provides /usr/bin/griabuntu-mail, the independent desktop/D-Bus/
schema identity io.github.d3rpapah0d3n.GriabuntuMail and the GriabuntuMail engine
namespace. New release profiles use ~/.config/griabuntu-mail,
~/.local/share/griabuntu-mail and ~/.cache/griabuntu-mail (or XDG equivalents).
The secret schema is separate too. No package script opens, copies, links or
removes an existing Convey/Flatpak profile or starts the application.

An upgrade from the first native preview removes its old package-owned launch
files. Per-user launcher overrides and any running old process must be handled
when deploying. Preserve old profiles and backups until an explicitly chosen
migration or fresh setup has been accepted; never copy a live mail database.

See docs/IDENTITY.md for the complete naming map, historical lookup exceptions
and old-path/new-path inventory. The current app/tray/symbolic envelope family derives from owner-supplied
ChatGPT output, installed from brand/ at native raster sizes. The supplied
originals do not inherit the earlier studies' CC0 claim; see
docs/ARTWORK-PROVENANCE.md. Earlier art remains archived under its own
terms. The native tonal UI is included; full desktop acceptance remains separate.
No public release, signing, source visibility change or automated publishing is
performed by this packaging. Native GUI acceptance is recorded separately from
headless regression tests.
